  ('saalbach-hinterglemm-austria', '01F', 'Saalbach-Hinterglemm', 'Austria', '270 km around the Skicircus, a World Championships pedigree', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Austria', '{"ski","entertainment","family","adventure","wellness","culinary"}', '{"alpine","festive","dramatic"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Skicircus Saalbach Hinterglemm Leogang Fieberbrunn = ~270 km pistes, ~69 lifts across 4 linked resorts (one of Austria''s largest)","Piste split ~52% easy (140 km) / 41% intermediate (112 km) / 7% difficult (18 km) - a family/intermediate mountain","''The Challenge'' = signature circular tour right around the Skicircus in a day (exact km/vertical to verify)","PROVINCE SEAM: Saalbach/Hinterglemm/Leogang = Salzburg; Fieberbrunn = Tirol (two provinces on one linked pass)","Hosted the FIS Alpine World Ski Championships 2025 (4-16 Feb) - 2nd time after 1991","Elevation 830-2,096 m (top Schattberg ~2,096 m); mid-altitude, backed by strong snowmaking; season ~late Nov-early April","''Best Austrian Apres-Ski'': Bauer''s Schi-Alm, Hinterhag Alm (''Melkstall''), Maisalm, Spitzbub, Der Jennerwein, Bobby''s Pub","Day pass ~EUR 79; Ski ALPIN CARD = up to 408 km with Zell am See-Kaprun + Schmittenhoehe; Epic tag on skiresort.info UNVERIFIED (not asserted); no Ikon","Village ~1,003 m, Glemmtal; deep ski-in/ski-out 4/5-star base; sunny south-facing slopes","Reached via Zell am See rail (~80 km S of Salzburg) + Glemmtal bus; Salzburg/Munich/Innsbruck airports","Fieberbrunn sector = freeride corner (former Freeride World Tour venue - verify)","Heli-skiing NOT available (Austria permits it only at Vorarlberg/Lech-Zurs sites)","Big summer mountain-biking + hiking destination on the same lifts","Nearest hospital = Tauernklinikum Zell am See (verify exact name/status)","Avalanche: Lawinenwarndienst Salzburg for the Salzburg sectors + Lawinenwarndienst Tirol for Fieberbrunn - EAWS 5-level, NOT SLF/Meteo"],"safety":{"emerge